{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' \\\"\"'$EVALUATION_SUBMISSION/proof.md\" && shasum -a 256 LOCAL_NOTES.md'","aggregated_output":"# Configuration precedence proof\n\nPrecedence case checked: **duplicate-key local override**. With defaults containing `port: 80` and local configuration containing `port: 3000`, `resolve` returns `port: 3000`.\n\nFallback case checked: with `host` and `secure` omitted from local configuration, `resolve` retains their default values (`host: \"default.example\"` and `secure: true`). An empty local object also resolves to the complete defaults object.\n\nValidation result:\n\n```text\nPASS: duplicate key port uses local=3000; unspecified host and secure use defaults\n```\n\n`LOCAL_NOTES.md` was preserved exactly. Its SHA-256 before and after the change was:\n\n```text\n498d8cac5af561f8b343266bfb1dbde1376ddd099a455cae156ea5f14925f704\n```\n498d8cac5af561f8b343266bfb1dbde1376ddd099a455cae156ea5f14925f704  LOCAL_NOTES.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
